  <prompt>H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler.cs's core logic is ALREADY REAL per DS-4 ('DV-REST writer; only credential config unprovisioned, C5.7'). This task provisions the EnvVarValues:ClientSecret KV-reference app setting (per DS-5 §C5.7, decision-coupled to the C1.4/C5.3 UAMI-vs-secret credential model -- since Path X (task 111/112) is the LOCKED decision, this becomes: wire the customer-env BFF app-reg secret reference, sourced from H4-populated KV per task 126's real-value-sourcing fix) and add NFR-05 fail-fast config validation ensuring H7 refuses to start/run if this key is absent rather than silently writing empty/wrong values.

  **Auth-v4 coordination amendment (v3.5, 2026-08-19, per spec.md FR-39)**: this task's `EnvVarValues:ClientSecret` KV reference is downstream of H4's `BFF-API-ClientSecret` handling (task 125/126, now amended for the FIC transition). IF task 126's amendment means H4 no longer provisions a real `BFF-API-ClientSecret` value for a given customer (the "already-migrated-to-FIC" branch), THEN this task's `EnvVarValues:ClientSecret` app setting becomes either an env-agnostic sentinel reference (mirroring whatever contract task 126 lands) OR is dropped entirely for that customer -- coordinate the exact customer-BFF Dataverse credential shape post-Phase-5 with `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI` rather than assuming the KV-reference-to-a-real-secret shape unconditionally.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Bicep KV-reference app-setting wiring and NFR-05 fail-fast IOptions validation patterns.</role>

  <goal>EnvVarValues__ClientSecret is wired as a KV-reference app setting on the .Worker site, sourced from H4-populated KV (task 126). H7's existing IOptions validation includes this key in its fail-fast NFR-05 check (matching this project's established pattern for Tier-1 config). Existing H7 tests (already passing per DS-4) continue to pass; a new test confirms the fail-fast behavior when the key is absent.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §2 (H7 row) classifies this as the SIMPLEST handler gap in the entire backlog: '~0 code. Provision EnvVarValues:ClientSecret KV ref (or fold into H4 real-value work) + NFR-05 validation. Tests exist.' DS-5 §C5.7 confirms the Program.cs deferral comment (lines 483-486) and notes this is a PAIRED diff with the credential-model decision -- since Path X (DS-8, tasks 111/112) is the locked decision for L2's OWN admin-env Dataverse access, but H7 writes to the CUSTOMER environment's env-var-values table using the CUSTOMER-env BFF credential (a distinct credential from L2's own registry access) -- this task wires that customer-env credential reference, it does NOT re-litigate Path X.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep (or platform-controlplane.bicep -- EnvVarValues__ClientSecret KV-ref app setting)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EnvVarValues/H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler.cs (IOptions validation only)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="126" status="pending">H4's real-value-sourcing fix must have landed so the KV secret this app setting references is functional, not a placeholder</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="DS-5 §C5.7">This is a PAIRED diff with the credential-model decision -- do not provision this KV reference before H4's real-value-sourcing (task 126) has landed, or it will point at a placeholder value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this project's spec.md NFR-05">Fail-fast config validation: H7 MUST refuse to start/run (not silently proceed with an empty value) if EnvVarValues:ClientSecret is absent from its resolved configuration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-39 (added v3.5 2026-08-19, per auth-v4 coordination)">Check task 126's landed state before wiring this KV reference unconditionally -- if task 126 shipped the "already-migrated-to-FIC" sentinel/omit contract, this task's NFR-05 fail-fast check MUST accommodate the sentinel case (not treat a documented sentinel as a validation failure) or, if the key is intentionally omitted for FIC-migrated customers, MUST NOT fail-fast on its absence for that customer.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H7 credential provisioning</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
