  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'EnvVarValues__ClientSecret' in the relevant Bicep module shows a KeyVault-reference app setting.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A new test confirms H7 fails fast (does not silently proceed) if EnvVarValues:ClientSecret is absent from configuration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing H7 tests (per DS-4, already passing) continue to pass unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If task 126 landed the "already-migrated-to-FIC" sentinel/omit contract for `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, a test confirms H7's fail-fast check does NOT trip on the documented sentinel value or the intentional absence for a FIC-migrated customer.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- H7's handler logic is already correct and real; this is purely a config-provisioning gap. Extension -- N/A, config wiring is not a code extension. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H7 cannot authenticate to write env-var values even though its logic is otherwise ready; H12c (downstream, needs H7's env-var definitions) stays blocked on a config gap alone.</notes>

  <notes-completion>
    Escalation trigger checked FIRST (per Wave G-4 dispatch owner directive, auth-v4 not started): the customer BFF's
    Dataverse credential path is NOT fully MI-based -- scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml still classifies
    "BFF-API-ClientSecret" as never_delete:true, value_source:"from-existing-kv" (a real, live secret). Escalation
    trigger does NOT fire; task executes per the base POML path, not the retirement path.

    Ground-truthed the KV-ref target: EnvVarValuesOptions.ClientSecret's doc comment (pre-existing, task 050) says H7
    authenticates using "the SAME identity + auth pattern H6 uses" -- the SHARED multitenant BFF app-reg (spec.md
    §9.1 v3 "one Spaarke tenant + one multitenant BFF app"), NOT a per-customer secret. This resolves to the platform
    KV's canonical "BFF-API-ClientSecret" secret (manifest.yaml), the SAME secret the .Api site already resolves as
    AzureAd__ClientSecret/Graph__ClientSecret -- confirmed via manifest.yaml cross-reference, not guessed.

    IMPLEMENTATION:
    1. EnvVarValuesOptions.cs (Core): added `SectionName = "EnvVarValues"` const (previously bound via bare
       `nameof(EnvVarValuesOptions)` = "EnvVarValuesOptions" -- renamed the section so the literal Bicep app-setting
       key matches the POML's own acceptance-criterion text `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` exactly; verified via
       InternalsVisibleTo that no other code/config depended on the old section name). Added `internal void Validate()`
       (parity with task 112/122's DataverseEnvironmentRegistryOptions.Validate() shape) checking ClientSecret
       non-empty + RequestTimeout in [1s,5m].
    2. Program.cs (Worker): replaced the plain `Configure<EnvVarValuesOptions>()` call with
       `AddOptions<T>().Bind(...).Validate(o => { o.Validate(); return true; }, "...").ValidateOnStart()` -- exact
       same pattern DataverseEnvironmentRegistryModule uses. Both layers retained: the handler's own existing runtime
       MissingClientSecret guard (returns Resumable Failure, does not crash) stays as defense-in-depth; the NEW
       boot-time ValidateOnStart() crashes the Worker at startup if a deployed environment is missing the setting --
       appropriate now that the Bicep wiring (step 3) makes this setting unconditional in every deploy, mirroring
       exactly how task 122 made DataverseEnvironmentRegistry required once its own unconditional registration landed.
    3. Bicep: added `bffApiClientSecretName` param (default 'BFF-API-ClientSecret') to both
       modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep and platform-controlplane.bicep (pass-through), and added the
       `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-reference app setting
       (`@Microsoft.KeyVault(VaultName=...;SecretName=${bffApiClientSecretName})`) to the Worker site's appSettings
       block, immediately after the existing DataverseEnvironmentRegistry block. Regenerated platform-controlplane.json
       via `az bicep build` (module has no separate compiled .json sibling). `az bicep build` on both files: 0
       errors, 0 warnings (net-new). Live `az deployment sub what-if` (dev subscription) returned status "Succeeded"
       -- the Worker App Service shows as a full Create (the live-ceremony Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 execution,
       backlog item #5, has not run yet against this environment -- expected, not a regression from this task); no
       new errors introduced.
    4. Tests: added 8 new test cases to H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandlerTests.cs's new "NFR-05" region --
       OptionsValidate_Throws_When_ClientSecret_Null, _Empty_Or_Whitespace (2 cases), _RequestTimeout_TooSmall (2
       cases), _RequestTimeout_TooLarge, _Passes_With_ClientSecret_And_Default_Timeout, and a
       _SectionName_Is_EnvVarValues regression-guard (ground-truths the Bicep app-setting-key contract so a future
       section-name drift fails at build time, not silently at deploy time). All call `options.Validate()` directly
       (parity with DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClientTests's "Options.Validate" region) -- ADR-038 Path #1 pure C#
       unit tests, no live HTTP/Dataverse round-trips, no banned Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.

    BONUS CATCH: adding `ValidateOnStart()` meant `IOptions&lt;EnvVarValuesOptions&gt;.Value` now throws eagerly
    whenever anything resolves it -- this would have SILENTLY BROKEN
    Dispatch/HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests.cs's WorkerTestFactory (task 103's "all 19 handlers resolve" DI
    completeness sweep constructs H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler, which takes IOptions&lt;EnvVarValuesOptions&gt; in
    its ctor) the moment it was next run, since that test host never previously set an EnvVarValues:ClientSecret
    placeholder. Caught by cross-referencing every existing site that had to add the equivalent
    `DataverseEnvironmentRegistry:AdminEnvironmentUrl` placeholder after task 122 landed the identical pattern (grep
    found exactly 2 sites: HandlerRegistrationCompletenessTests.cs and ProvisioningDispatchSpineSeamTests.cs). Fixed
    the first (adds the placeholder, same convention). Verified the second does NOT need it -- its SeamTestFactory
    only ever resolves the scripted "H1" canary handler + IHandlerEnqueuer, never H7 or EnvVarValuesOptions (confirmed
    via grep of the whole test file) -- so no change was needed there; would have been a wasted/misleading setting
    otherwise.

    Acceptance criterion 5 (FIC sentinel/omit accommodation) is N/A for this landed state -- see escalation-trigger
    check above; not implemented since no sentinel contract exists to accommodate yet (avoided speculative code for a
    hypothetical future contract per CLAUDE.md §11 cost-of-doing-nothing discipline).

    Tests: 938 -&gt; 946/946 (+8, zero regressions, all 23 pre-existing H7 test methods unmodified). `dotnet build`
    0 errors/0 warnings (Core+Worker). No new NuGet packages -&gt; no CVE scan needed. Step 9.5 (code-review +
    adr-check, test-modifying override): 0 Critical, 0 Warnings, 0 ADR violations -- no interfaces added (ADR-010),
    no hardcoded secrets (grep-verified), no BFF-hygiene trigger (L2 control-plane only, not
    src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**).
  </notes-completion>

